 { The presence of opposite-coloured bishops often saves the defender even if he is a pawn down, but here Black is suffering from a bad structure - his queenside pawns are effectively parried by the opposing minority, whereas White doesn't have the same problem on the opposite flank. Imagine the c6-pawn on f7 instead and Black should have no difficulties in making a draw. } 1. { -KEY- } g4 $1 { Smyslov opts for the only plan that can threaten Black: the creation of connected passed pawns on the e- and f-files. } ( { Note that } 1. Kg5 Kf7 2. f4 $2 { ( 2.g4! works fine, in similar fashion to the game) would let Black blockade the pawns by } Bc2 $1 3. e5 Ke6 { with an easy draw. } ) 
hxg4 ( { Or } 1... Bd1 2. gxh5 gxh5 3. Ke3 $1 { followed by f3-f4-f5. } ) 
2. Kxg4 $1 ( 2. fxg4 $2 Bd1 { is less promising; e.g. } 3. Bd4 Be2 4. Kg5 Kf7 $1 5. h5 gxh5 6. gxh5 Bf3 7. e5 Be4 { with good drawing chances. } ) 
Bd1 3. Kf4 { The next part of White's plan is to push h4-h5, but first he should improve his king and bishop. } Kf7 4. Bd4 Kf8 5. Ke3 ( { Speeding up the plan used in the game by } 5. h5 $5 gxh5 6. Bf2 { followed by Ke3 and f3-f4 was also possible. Actually already on move 4, White could play h5, as observed by c0rias. } ) 
Kf7 6. Be5 Ke6 7. Bg3 $1 { From here the bishop will control the black kingside pawn once the h4-h5 sacrifice is effected. } Kf6 ( { After } 7... Kd7 8. h5 $1 gxh5 9. f4 c5 $5 10. bxc5 Kc6 11. Kd4 Kb5 12. f5 { White should be winning - Smyslov. } ) 
8. Bf4 Ke6 ( { Or } 8... Bb3 9. Bg5 Ke6 10. h5 $1 gxh5 11. f4 { with similar play. } ) 
9. h5 $1 { The connected passed pawns are finally created. } gxh5 10. Bg3 ( { After } 10. Bg3 { Black resigned since further resistance is useless; e.g. } Bc2 ( { but let's notice that if all the pawns were stripped from the board, apart from the ones on e4 and f3 , then Black would draw by } 10. Bg3 Ba4 { followed by ...Bd7-c8-d7; as already mentioned, the more pawns on the board, the better (usually) for the attacker } ) 
11. f4 Bb1 12. f5 Kf7 13. Kf4 Bc2 14. e5 Bb3 15. Kg5 { or } 15. e6 ) 

 1-0

